# Intent

Maintain consistent component structure and file placement in the domain-first architecture.

# Rules

## A) File Structure

- ✅ `/src/app/` -> Next.js routes and route layouts only
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/core/` -> business schemas, rules, ports, use cases
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/infrastructure/` -> domain adapters, repositories, mappers
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/presentation/components/` -> domain-specific UI pieces
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/presentation/hooks/` -> domain React Query hooks
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/presentation/stores/` -> domain UI state
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/presentation/pages/` -> domain route-level pages
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/presentation/layouts/` -> domain route-level layouts
- ✅ `/src/domains/<domain>/presentation/navigation/` -> domain navigation config
- ✅ `/src/shared/design-system/ui/` -> reusable UI primitives
- ✅ `/src/shared/a11y/` -> reusable accessibility utilities
- ✅ `/src/styles/` -> global styles and variables

## B) Route Files (`src/app`)

scope: file.path matches ^src/app/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** keep route files focused on route composition
- ✅ **ALWAYS** use `page.tsx` and `layout.tsx` conventions
- ✅ **ALWAYS** delegate route UI to domain pages or layouts when the route is domain-specific
- ❌ **NEVER** put domain business rules in route files
- ❌ **NEVER** call Supabase directly from route files

## C) Reusable UI Primitives (`src/shared/design-system/ui`)

scope: file.path matches ^src/shared/design-system/ui/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** place reusable primitives here
- ✅ **ALWAYS** keep them domain-agnostic
- ✅ **ALWAYS** reuse `src/shared/a11y/` utilities where needed
- ❌ **NEVER** embed ticket, board, epic, sprint, or other domain logic here
- ❌ **NEVER** fetch data directly in reusable UI primitives

## D) Domain-Specific Components

scope: file.path matches ^src/domains/.+/presentation/components/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** place domain-specific UI in the owning domain
- ✅ **ALWAYS** organize a component in its own folder when it has styles or helpers
- ✅ **ALWAYS** receive ready data via props or domain hooks
- ❌ **NEVER** move shared primitives here when they belong in `src/shared/design-system/ui/`
- ❌ **NEVER** call Supabase directly from components

## E) Domain Hooks

scope: file.path matches ^src/domains/.+/presentation/hooks/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** place React Query hooks inside the owning domain
- ✅ **ALWAYS** call domain use cases from hooks
- ❌ **NEVER** call shared infrastructure clients directly when a domain repository exists
- ❌ **NEVER** treat hooks as a replacement for domain rules or use cases

## F) Domain Stores

scope: file.path matches ^src/domains/.+/presentation/stores/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** keep stores for UI state only
- ✅ **ALWAYS** scope stores to the owning domain
- ❌ **NEVER** place business rules in stores
- ❌ **NEVER** call Supabase directly from stores

## G) Domain Pages and Layouts

scope: file.path matches ^src/domains/.+/presentation/(pages|layouts)/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** place route-level domain composition here
- ✅ **ALWAYS** use semantic HTML structure
- ✅ **ALWAYS** compose shared design-system primitives and domain hooks
- ❌ **NEVER** put reusable design-system primitives here

## H) Styling

scope: file.path matches ^src/(app|domains|shared/design-system/ui)/.+\.(ts|tsx)$

- ✅ **ALWAYS** use SCSS modules or shared global styles from `src/styles/`
- ✅ **ALWAYS** use variables from `src/styles/variables/*`
- ❌ **NEVER** hardcode colors, spacing, or sizing values
- ❌ **NEVER** use inline styles by default

# Auto-suggestions

- If reusable UI is inside a domain -> **Move to `src/shared/design-system/ui/`**
- If route file contains business logic -> **Move logic into the owning domain module**
- If hook is global and domain-specific -> **Move it to `src/domains/<domain>/presentation/hooks/`**
- If store contains business logic -> **Move logic into a domain use case or rule**
